--- v37/docs/art/stitch_drone/prompts.json
+++ v38/docs/art/stitch_drone/prompts.json
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+{
+  "hover": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: production 2D game enemy animation spritesheet, RGBA transparent background. Create ONE square spritesheet with exactly 9 frames in a perfectly regular 3 columns by 3 rows grid, equal invisible cells, row-major looping hover animation. Every frame is the SAME small original Stitch Drone repair robot, viewed from a fixed elevated three-quarter angle facing left. Character design: compact floating brass-and-dark-iron sewing spool body, bright cyan thread wound around its central spool, two curved suture-needle antennae projecting upward, tiny cyan lens, two small articulated repair pincers folded beside the body, a small downward hover emitter. Distinct narrow flying silhouette; no legs, no cannon, no beetle body. Hand-painted high-quality crisp game sprite style, thick dark contours, worn bronze rims, subtle teal enamel panels, warm highlights, readable at 57 pixels tall; not photoreal, not smooth vector. All 9 frames keep identical design, camera, scale and palette, gently bobbing 2–4 pixels while antennae and hover emission cycle. Image must have genuine alpha transparency with no background, no ground shadow, no text, no frames or grid lines, no labels, no watermark, no extra objects. Center each entire character within its own equal cell, occupy only central 55% of each cell width and height, generous fully transparent margin on all sides. No cropped antennae or overlapping frames. This is the neutral hover/move cycle, not an attack or death.",
